%h1 Instructor Guide: Specifying Due Dates
%p
  CodeWorkout uses a YAML-based interface for managing workout availability and student extensions. This allows you to quickly set up schedules for multiple sections and handle individual student needs in a single, human-readable view.

%h2 1. Workout Offering Dates
%p
  Each section of a course has three primary date fields:
%ul
  %li
    %b due:
    The main due date (soft deadline). Students can still submit after this date if a hard deadline is set.
  %li
    %b from:
    The opening date. The workout becomes visible and accessible at this time. Use 
    %code always
    if you want it available immediately.
  %li
    %b until:
    The hard deadline. Submissions are completely blocked after this time. If not specified, it defaults to 
    %code +0 minutes
    (meaning the workout closes exactly at the due date).

%h2 2. Relative Offsets
%p
  Instead of entering full date/time strings, you can use relative offsets from the 
  %code due
  date. This is especially useful for setting up consistent schedules across sections.
%ul
  %li
    %b Flexible Units:
    You can use 
    %code minutes
    (or 
    %code min
    ), 
    %code hours
    (or 
    %code hr
    ), 
    %code days
    (or 
    %code d
    ), or 
    %code weeks
    (or 
    %code w
    ).
  %li
    %b Opening Dates (from):
    These must be negative. You can use a leading 
    %code -
    sign (e.g., 
    %code -3 days
    ) or no sign at all (e.g., 
    %code 1 week
    will be interpreted as 
    %code -1 week
    ).
  %li
    %b Hard Deadlines (until):
    These must be non-negative. You can use a leading 
    %code +
    sign (e.g., 
    %code +12 hours
    ) or no sign at all (e.g., 
    %code 1 day
    will be interpreted as 
    %code +1 day
    ).

%h3 Example Configuration:
%pre.examples
  :preserve
    sections:
      - section: CS 101 Section A
        due: 2025-09-15 11:59 PM
        from: 1 week           # Opens 1 week before due date
        until: +2 days         # Closes 2 days after due date
      - section: CS 101 Section B
        due: 2025-09-16 11:59 PM
        from: always           # Always open
        until: +0 minutes      # Closes exactly at due date

%h2 3. Student Extensions
%p
  Student extensions allow you to override the default dates for specific students. You can group multiple students who share the same extension dates.
%ul
  %li
    Extensions use the same 
    %code due
    , 
    %code from
    , and 
    %code until
    rules as regular offerings.
  %li
    Students can be specified by their full name and email (e.g., 
    %code John Doe <jdoe@example.edu>
    ) or just their email.

%h3 Example Extensions:
%pre.examples
  :preserve
    extensions:
      - due: 2025-09-20 11:59 PM
        from: always
        until: +0 minutes
        students:
          - Alice Smith <asmith@example.edu>
          - Bob Jones <bjones@example.edu>
      - due: +3 days           # 3 days after their original section due date
        from: -1 week
        until: +1 day
        students:
          - charlie@example.edu

%h2 4. Tips for Success
%ul
  %li
    %b Time Zones:
    All absolute dates are interpreted in your current time zone (as set in your profile).
  %li
    %b Validation:
    The system will notify you if you enter an invalid student or an impossible relative offset (like a positive 
    %code from
    date).
  %li
    %b Human Readable:
    When you save the form, the system will clean up your YAML to ensure it uses standardized units and explicit signs for clarity.
